{
 "about": "Which wildcard dialect MATCH speaks on a path. The agent's own condition parser accepts every pattern here and hands it on as a string, and four answers are recorded for the operator: x5-match-unquoted-wildcard has ab* matching abc, not matching xabc and not matching ABC, so MATCH is anchored and case-sensitive; a2-match-attribute-pattern has a pattern taken from an attribute answering false; and x34-regex-literal has /ab.*/ answering false even for a value the regex describes. Nothing before these cases says what a metacharacter does to a path separator. Every case sends a URI the pattern should select and a URI it should not, so a pattern access-control accepts and never evaluates shows as a column of false answers rather than as a dialect. md7-pattern-without-a-metacharacter is the control for the whole file: its pattern carries no metacharacter, so a false answer on uri-equal means the attribute path or the operand order is wrong and no other answer in the file means anything.",
 "resourceTypePrefix": "PARITY_SUITE_MATCH_",
 "pins": {},
 "pips": {},
 "cases": [
